{"kind": "mod", "id": 1716, "name": "WTT - Armory - IWI Carmel", "slug": "wtt-armory-iwi-carmel", "teaser": "IWI's latest 5.56 NATO rifle has arrived in Tarkov", "owner_name": "Tron", "downloads": 20257, "favourites": 0, "featured": false, "contains_ads": true, "contains_ai_content": false, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": null, "guid": null, "thumbnail_local": null, "category": null, "category_id": null, "updated_at": "2026-07-07T16:59:01.000000Z", "created_at": "2024-09-05T16:53:29.000000Z", "published_at": "2024-09-05T16:53:29.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~3.10.0", "latest_version": "1.0.1", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": null, "description_html": "<div class=\"tabset\"><div id=\"tabset-1-panel-1\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Mod Description</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.ibb.co/sV8dKhN/Carmel1.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/sV8dKhN/Carmel1.png\" alt=\"Carmel1.png\" /></a></p>\n<p>IWI’s latest 5.56 NATO rifle has arrived in Tarkov.</p>\n<p>This was a collaborative project between 3D modeler Civok and the WTT team.</p>\n<p>The 3D model and textures of this weapon were created from scratch by Civok.</p>\n<p>I reworked a lot of the animations on this container to make it look right.</p>\n<p>Thanks to Rexana for the textures on the new MBUS 3 iron sights.</p>\n<p>Thanks to both Ehtacs and Moloc for balancing.</p>\n<p>You can find Civok in the WTT discord where he periodically shares renders of his work.</p>\n<p>This is one of many small content standalone weapon packs that I will be releasing. These are meant to be lightweight and compatible with <em><strong>most</strong></em> other mods.</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.ibb.co/8MnS9LD/Carmel2.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/8MnS9LD/Carmel2.png\" alt=\"Carmel2.png\" /></a></p>\n<p>-------------------------------------</p>\n<p>The rifle along with its attachments can be found at Skier LL2.</p>\n<p>-------------------------------------</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.ibb.co/VY93mS5/Carmel5.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/VY93mS5/Carmel5.png\" alt=\"Carmel5.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.ibb.co/pL0NJKy/Carmel3.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/pL0NJKy/Carmel3.png\" alt=\"Carmel3.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.ibb.co/qJsYJGD/Carmel4.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/qJsYJGD/Carmel4.png\" alt=\"Carmel4.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.ibb.co/fFtzyHh/Carmel6.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/fFtzyHh/Carmel6.png\" alt=\"Carmel6.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.ibb.co/ZWQHPJb/Carmel-Inventory.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/ZWQHPJb/Carmel-Inventory.png\" alt=\"Carmel-Inventory.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.ibb.co/TYvqc0M/carmelfdeinventory.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/TYvqc0M/carmelfdeinventory.png\" alt=\"carmelfdeinventory.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><strong>WTT- ARMORY - REALISM COMPATIBILITY</strong></p>\n<p>WTT Armory weapons will work with Realism properly if they are added to Realism’s database.</p>\n<p>The link below will take you to Fontaine’s (Creator of Realism) documentation on how to properly implement weapons/items/equipment into Realism.</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/doc/entry/88-realism-mod-adding-compatibility-for-weapons-gear-and-ammo/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Fontaine’s Documentation on Adding Realism Compatibility</a></p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-2\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">What is WTT?</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>What is Welcome To Tarkov?</strong></p>\n<p>Welcome To Tarkov (WTT) is a mod for SPT AKI that has been in development for over a year. What started as a small passion project has grown in size to incorporate 10+ core members as well as contributions from other well-known mod authors and friends of WTT alike.</p>\n<p><strong>How does Welcome To Tarkov change the game?</strong></p>\n<p>As a mod, WTT overhauls SPT AKI, touching on almost every vanilla game system, as well as adding completely new systems to the game and its core mechanics. Inspired by open-world hardcore survival projects like STALKER: Anomaly and STALKER: GAMMA, WTT takes SPT’s artificial multiplayer MMO difficulty adders and replaces them with a challenging world economy, loot scarcity rebalancing, a lore friendly quest overhaul, and a map-traveling system built from rewritten portions of the Traveler mod allowing seamless travel between maps. Aside from its changes to the game’s core properties, WTT also adds to the world’s variety of traders, NPC’s, characters, items, and quests:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Over 500 custom bundles adding new weapons, attachments, wearables, containers, food, medical, and barter items.</li>\n<li>New bosses with their own custom gear that will be properly incorporated into WTT’s quest lines.</li>\n<li>New, meaningful traders with their own lore-friendly quests and narrative elements to help the player progress through the story-line of WTT.</li>\n<li>New playable characters and outfits that will add to the player’s customization abilities.</li>\n<li>New quest types incorporating brand new map extraction points, putting the player’s knowledge and familiarization of SPT’s maps to the test.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Welcome To Tarkov stands as one of the largest mods created for SPT AKI thus far.</p>\n<p><strong>When does Welcome To Tarkov release?</strong></p>\n<p><em>Thursday.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Which Thursday?</strong></p>\n<p><em>TBD</em></p>\n<p><strong>Want to follow our progress?</strong></p>\n<p>You can follow the project through it’s development in our discord here:</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://discord.gg/Nz6VX78xRa\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://discord.gg/Nz6VX78xRa</a></p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-3\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">WTT Standalone Mods</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1788-wtt-head-and-voice-selector/?highlight=wtt\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/whtTRh9/Head-And-Voice-Selector.png\" alt=\"Head-And-Voice-Selector.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1790-wtt-pack-n-strap/?highlight=wtt#overview\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/znRTpS4/Pack-NStrap.png\" alt=\"Pack-NStrap.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1818-wtt-little-drummer-boy/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Hz4dR3S/drummer.png\" alt=\"drummer.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1317-wtt-rogue-justice/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/D90vct1/rogue.png\" alt=\"rogue.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href